# laser3015 with the gantry link between its Y drives (the default gains)
# laser3015: an imaginary 3 x 1.5 m fiber laser flatbed from the 2000s,
# retrofitted: its linear-motor gantry and scales kept, the drives and the
# controller replaced by stmbl and LinuxCNC. The gantry runs along the 3 m
# (Y) on two iron-core Baldor LMBL18B (one per side), the cutting head's
# carriage on an LMBL14B along the 1.5 m bridge (X). Iron-core motors cog
# (45.72 mm period: a ripple every half of it). The welded frame carries a
# slat table and stands on six levelling feet. Masses, modes and friction
# are made up, of a plausible size.
#@dynwiz 10000 10000 1500
drive y1 laser3015_y_glink.conf ../sim.txt 45.72
drive y2 laser3015_y_glink.conf ../sim.txt 45.72
drive x laser3015_x.conf ../sim.txt 45.72
origin 750 1500
stroke -5 3005 -5 1505
frame 4500 6150 15 13 16 0.05
rails 1.9
# a welded steel bridge 1.9 m long, the carriage with its Z axis and the
# cutting head (the head's own modes: on its Z slide and the bridge)
bridge 110 33
carriage 22 0.15
racking 2e6 0.02
head 14 0.08 38 42 19 0.025
# bellows and two heavy cable chains
guidey 60 120
guidex 35 40
cogging y1 28 22.86 30
cogging y2 26 22.86 75
cogging x 18 22.86 0
# the supply's 2200 uF and the drives' own 3 x 470 uF; a brake chopper
bus 3610 230 0.5 360 22
# the Y drives' gantry link: 600 us latency, a frame every 400 us (2.5 kHz CAN)
glink 3 2
home 750 1500
